  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICMPS 2025 PBI Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &quot;Defence of the right to defend rights, life and territory&quot; project in Mexico implemented by Peace Brigades International,  offers an international accompaniment model (physical and political) to organisations, individuals and communities who are at risk due to their legitimate work in defending human rights and/or who have been victims of serious human rights violations. The project opens and maintains spaces for human rights defenders, particularly a regional forum for exchange between women defenders from Mesoamerica (Mexico, Guatemala, Honduras, Nicaragua) and Colombia, where they can learn about the realities of their struggles for territory in the context of extractive mega-infraestructure projects that are destroying their territories.</narrative>
  </description>
